# Git commits

Commit on your own after completing individual tasks, fixes, or review items — do not wait for the user to ask.

## When to commit

- One commit per logical task or fix (not one giant commit at the end)
- After finishing a review fix, commit that fix before moving to the next
- Include formatting-only changes (e.g. `cargo fmt`) in the same commit as the related code change

## Format

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/): `type(scope): subject`

Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `chore`, `ci`, `perf`

## The juxtaposition

Every commit is a **feral subject, serious body** bit. Crank the dial.

- **Subject**: maximum unhinged gen-z / brainrot. Lowercase. Slang pile-up. Memes. Sound like a sleep-deprived group chat that just discovered git. If a sober engineer would write that subject, rewrite it dumber. Prefer chaos over clever.
- **Emoji**: encouraged throughout the subject (not required). Sprinkle freely — 💀🔥😭🤡💅✨🚨 etc. Emoji may **optionally replace words** (`died` → `💀`, `fire` → `🔥`, `no cap` energy via 🧢). Do not force one in every commit; when they fit the bit, lean in. Body stays emoji-free unless quoting user-facing copy.
- **Body**: crisp, professional engineering prose. What changed, why, trade-offs. Complete sentences. Could go in a PR description or postmortem. Zero slang here.

The contrast is the entire joke. Subject = TikTok comment section. Body = staff engineer.

```bash
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
fix(chat): bestie the websocket literally ate shit and 💀

The handler assumed every inbound message included a user ID. Anonymous
viewer messages omitted the field and caused a panic in the parser.
Guard the optional field and skip processing when absent.

EOF
)"
```

More subject examples (body always stays normal):

- `feat(overlay): we cooked so hard the badge renderer is giving sigma grindset fr fr 🔥`
- `fix(auth): token refresh was lowkey feral and not in a good way like at all 😭`
- `refactor(db): yeeted duplicate query into one function no thoughts head empty 🧠❌`
- `chore(deps): bumped tokio bc living in 2023 is literally not the vibe anymore`
- `feat(tracker): hall of shame just unlocked and chat is about to be so washed 🚽`
- `fix(ping): templates were catching bodies with the cr lf split no 🧢`

**Anti-patterns for subjects** (too tame — rewrite):

- `feat(tracker): add hall of shame commands` ← corporate. trash it.
- `fix(auth): improve token refresh handling` ← LinkedIn. trash it.
- Anything a changelog bot would write unchanged.
- Sterile subjects that avoid slang *and* emoji when either would land the bit.

## Safety

Follow the git safety protocol: never push to `main`, no `--no-verify`, no committing secrets, no amend unless explicitly allowed.
